UPDATE companies SET description='Unverferth Manufacturing Co., Inc. began in 1948 when Lawrence G. and Richard Unverferth launched L.G. Unverferth Manufacturing in Kalida, Ohio, with a family loan secured by war bonds. Their first products were combine shucker levers and a patented bolt‑on dual‑wheel extension that founded the company’s wheel‑system business. The firm remains family‑owned; its corporate headquarters are now in Casselton, North Dakota, while the Kalida campus handles design, engineering, fabrication, welding, powder coating and assembly.

Eight sales and distribution branches in the U.S. and Canada support the six brands.

Blu‑Jet focuses on anhydrous ammonia and liquid fertilizer application; Brent leads high‑capacity grain carts; Orthman supplies strip‑till and toolbar systems; Top Air builds pull‑type and self‑propelled sprayers with T‑Tank and steerable‑hitch technology; and the Unverferth brand covers wheel systems, seed handling and tillage.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product design and engineering", "Precision machining", "Fabrication", "Welding", "Powder coating", "Assembly", "Grain cart and wagon manufacturing", "Header transport manufacturing", "Seed tender manufacturing", "Fertilizer applicator manufacturing", "Tillage equipment manufacturing", "Auger and conveyor manufacturing", "Agricultural wheel system manufacturing"], "industries": ["Agriculture", "Agricultural machinery", "Spraying", "Fertilizer application", "Tillage", "Grain handling", "Seed handling"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": [], "facts_used": ["Founded 1948 in Kalida, Ohio by Lawrence G. and Richard Unverferth -> /about-us", "Family-owned and operated -> /about-us", "Corporate headquarters in Casselton, North Dakota -> db", "Four manufacturing locations and eight sales/distribution branches across U.S. and Canada -> / (home page)", "Six brands: Blu-Jet, Brent, Orthman, Parker, Top Air, Unverferth -> / (home page)", "Product portfolio: grain carts, wagons, header transports, seed tenders, fertilizer applicators, tillage equipment, augers, conveyors, wheel systems -> /about-us", "Processes: product design, engineering, fabrication, welding, powder coating, assembly -> /about-us (Kalida facility description)", "Precision machining, welding, fabrication at Delphos facility -> description (db)", "Industries: spraying industry -> industries_served", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Unverferth Manufacturing Co., Inc. is a family-owned and operated agricultural equipment manufacturer producing a wide range of products that help the farming community be more efficient.", "founded_year": "1948", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/unverferth-manufacturing-co.-inc./"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='unverferth-manufacturing-co-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Urschel Laboratories was founded in 1910 in Valparaiso, Indiana, by William E. Urschel, who invented the Gooseberry Snipper to automate a labor-intensive hand process. The company relocated to Chesterton, Indiana, and remained a privately held family business for four generations until March 3, 2016, when the Urschel family sold the company to its employees through an Employee Stock Ownership Plan (ESOP), making it 100 percent employee-owned. Patrick Urschel serves as CEO.

The company designs and manufactures industrial food cutting machines, including dicers, slicers, shredders, and milling equipment. Its product line performs slicing, dicing, strip cutting, shredding, granulating, milling, and pureeing for high-volume food processors. Current models include the Little Gem Aspire™ Dicer, M VersaPro® Dicer, DiversaCut 2110A® Dicer, Sprint 2® Dicer, and several Affinity® series dicers. Urschel also distributes KRONEN commercial processing systems in the U.S., Mexico, Pakistan, China, Italy, and across Asia.

Urschel serves the food processing and allied industries, supplying equipment to processors of fruits, vegetables, potatoes, meat, cheese, baked goods, nut products, and pet food. The company reports a presence in more than 130 countries.

Urschel attributes its differentiation to its in-house Innovation & Development team, which develops patented cutting technologies through extensive R&D, and to its employee-ownership culture, which the company says aligns every team member with long-term customer success.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Slicing", "Dicing", "Strip cutting", "Shredding", "Granulating", "Milling", "Pureeing", "Comitrol processing", "Equipment manufacturing", "Research and development", "Global distribution and service"], "industries": ["Food processing", "Fruit and vegetable processing", "Potato processing", "Meat processing", "Cheese processing", "Bakery", "Pet food manufacturing", "Nut processing", "Commercial food processing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Little Gem Aspire\u2122 Dicer", "M VersaPro\u00ae Dicer", "DiversaCut 2110A\u00ae Dicer", "Sprint 2\u00ae Dicer", "DiversaCut Sprint\u00ae Dicer", "Affinity\u00ae Dicer", "Affinity Integra\u00ae Dicer", "Affinity\u00ae Integra-D Dicer", "Affinity\u00ae CD-L Dicer", "Model M6 Dicer", "Dicers", "Slicers", "Shredders", "Milling equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% employee-owned (ESOP) since 2016", "Patented cutting technology developed by in-house Innovation & Development team", "Global reach: 130+ countries served", "Four generations of family leadership before ESOP conversion", "Offers KRONEN commercial processing systems in key international markets"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1910 in Valparaiso, Indiana by William E. Urschel -> /", "Headquartered in Chesterton, Indiana -> db", "100% employee-owned via ESOP since March 3, 2016 -> /", "Patrick Urschel is CEO -> /", "Manufactures industrial food cutting machines (dicers, slicers, shredders, milling equipment) -> /", "Processes: slicing, dicing, strip cutting, shredding, granulating, milling, pureeing, comitrol processing -> /", "Product models: Little Gem Aspire Dicer, M VersaPro Dicer, DiversaCut 2110A Di