UPDATE companies SET description='The shop provides complete steel fabrication, from design and engineering through installation. Its AISC-, ASME- and AWS-certified welders perform MIG, TIG and flux-core welding. CNC plasma cutting runs on a Burn Table and an Inovatech 600 Beamline powered by Hypertherm. An on-site blast and paint booth handles sand, soda and hydro blasting plus epoxy, urethane, irathane and Duromar coatings. The detailing department works in BIM and CAD using Tekla, Advanced Steel and AutoCAD, with senior designers holding over 50 years of combined experience. Field services are delivered through Tekko, Inc., the company''s installation arm, whose staff brings more than 100 years of heavy-industrial construction background in mining, power and oil & gas.

Utah Fabrication serves municipalities, mining operations, energy producers, transportation agencies, power plants, oil & gas facilities, heavy-industrial sites and marine projects across the western United States and has shipped work internationally.

The company states it was started to provide a "best in class" value product and service while ensuring a rewarding, safe workplace and acting as a benefit to its communities. Its stated values are integrity, accountability and respect, with an emphasis on inspecting what is expected.', certifications=ARRAY['ASME','AISC','AWS','NACE']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "MIG welding", "TIG welding", "Flux-core welding", "CNC plasma cutting", "Sand blasting", "Soda blasting", "Hydro blasting", "Epoxy coating", "Urethane coating", "Industrial specialty coatings (Irathanes, Duromar)", "Structural steel detailing", "BIM/CAD modeling", "Tekla modeling", "Advanced Steel modeling", "AutoCAD drafting", "Field installation services", "Turnkey project management"], "industries": ["Municipalities", "Mining", "Energy", "Transportation", "Power generation", "Oil & Gas", "Heavy industrial", "Marine"], "materials": ["Structural steel", "Industrial steel", "Miscellaneous steel", "Epoxies", "Urethanes", "Irathanes", "Duromar"], "equipment": ["Burn Table", "Inovatech 600 Beamline Powered by Hypertherm", "Blast and paint booth facility"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AISC, ASME and AWS certified welders", "CNC plasma cutting via Burn Table and Inovatech 600 Beamline (Hypertherm)", "On-site blast and paint booth for sand, soda and hydro blasting", "NACE Certified Coatings Engineer and HAZMAT Technician on staff", "MSHA and Confined Space trained personnel", "50+ years combined detailing experience (Tekla, Advanced Steel, AutoCAD)", "100+ years construction background for field installation through Tekko, Inc."], "facts_used": ["Location: Tooele, Utah -> db", "Founding principle: best product at reasonable price, strong work ethic -> /", "Industries served: Municipalities, Mining, Energy, Transportation, Power, Oil & Gas, Heavy Industrial, Marine -> /", "International shipping -> /", "AISC, ASME, AWS certified welders -> /", "Welding processes: MIG, TIG, flux core -> /", "CNC plasma cutting: Burn Table, Inovatech 600 Beamline (Hypertherm) -> /", "Finishing: sandblasting, epoxy, urethane coating -> /", "Design/engineering: BIM/CAD, Tekla, Advanced Steel, AutoCAD, 50+ years combined experience -> /", "Paint/sandblasting: on-site booth, sand/soda/hydro blasting, epoxies/urethanes/irathanes/Duromar -> /", "NACE Certified Coatings Engineer, HAZMAT Technician -> /", "Staff MSHA and Confined Space trained -> /", "Field services via Tekko, Inc., 100+ years construction background -> /", "ASME certification listed -> db", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Utah Fabrication has fabricated steel components for a wide array of industries including but not limited to Municipalities, Mining, Energy and Transportation Sectors", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["shipped internationally"], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/utah-fabrication/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='utah-fabrication' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Uzelac Industries was founded in 2003 by Michael Uzelac in Greendale, Wisconsin, after he acquired Poja Sheetmetal (established 1956) and later Duske Engineering (established 1980).

The company designs and manufactures custom direct-fired rotary drying systems, each engineered to a customer’s specific process requirements. In addition to its core dryer line, Uzelac provides contract fabrication for large equipment OEMs, offering brake bending, rolling, shearing, punching, MIG/TIG welding, and waterjet cutting from a plant equipped with 25-ton and 10-ton crane bays. Its workforce consists of journeyman fabricators and engineers with 40-plus years of experience, and the firm holds several U.S. patents on dryer design.

Uzelac serves the hemp, poultry, biomass, rendering, biosolids, and gasification sectors. In poultry, it has supplied rotary dryers to Herbruck’s Poultry Ranch, Michael Foods, Foster Farms, and Tyson for over 30 years. Its systems also support anaerobic digestion and bioenergy projects worldwide, with installations across multiple countries.

The business was built on the shared values of integrity, customer satisfaction, and innovation inherited from Industrial MetalFab Specialties and Duske Drying Systems. Michael Uzelac’s vision combined the craftsmanship of Poja Sheetmetal with Duske’s custom engineering to create a specialist in direct-fired rotary technology, a focus that remains central to the company’s identity today.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom direct-fired rotary dryer design and manufacturing", "Contract fabrication for large equipment OEMs", "Turnkey equipment fabrication", "Brake bending and rolling", "Shearing and punching", "MIG and TIG welding", "Waterjet cutting", "Custom fabrication", "Low-quantity complex fabrication", "Stainless steel fabrication and welding", "Aluminum fabrication and welding", "Hot-rolled and cold-rolled steel fabrication and welding", "Factory-assembled rotary dryer systems", "Onsite assembly for large dryer systems", "Engineering design of customized drying systems"], "industries": ["Hemp", "Poultry", "Biomass", "Rendering", "Biosolids", "Gasification", "Anaerobic digestion", "Bioenergy"], "materials": ["Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Hot-rolled steel", "Cold-rolled steel"], "equipment": ["25-ton crane bay (22.5 ft clear under hook)", "10-ton crane bay (22.5 ft clear under hook)", "Waterjet cutting system", "Brake bending and rolling equipment", "Shearing and punching equipment", "MIG and TIG welding equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom direct-fired rotary dryers designed and built per customer specifications", "Factory-assembled dryers requiring minimal installation or onsite assembly for larger systems", "In-house fabrication capabilities including brake bending, rolling, shearing, punching, MIG/TIG welding, and waterjet cutting", "Several U.S. patents on rotary dryer design", "Family-owned with leadership transition to next generation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2003 by Michael Uzelac after acquiring Poja Sheetmetal and Duske Engineering -> /about", "Family-owned, leadership transition to next generation -> /", "Headquarters moved from Greendale to Pewaukee, Wisconsin -> /", "Specializes in custom direct-fired rotary drying systems -> /", "Provides fabrication services for large equipment OEMs -> /", "Facility: 17,100 sq ft with 25-ton and 10-ton crane bays -> /about", "Processes: brake bending, rolling, shearing, punching, MIG/TIG welding, waterjet cutting -> /about", "Workforce: journeyman fabricators with 40+ years experience -> /about", "Engineering staff with 40+ years experience custom-designing systems -> /about", "Holds several U.S. patents on dryer design -> /about", "Industries served: hemp, poultry, biomass, rendering, biosolids, gasification -> /", "Poultry clients: Herbruck\u2019s Poultry Ranch, Michael Foods, Foster Farms, Tyson -> /", "Global installations -> /about", "Core values: integrity, customer satisfaction, innovation -> /about", "Predecessor companies: Industrial MetalFab Specialties (Poja, 1956) and Duske Drying Systems (Duske Engineering, 1980) -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Uzelac Industries specializes in engineering, design, and manufacturing custom direct-fired rotary drying systems. In addition to the core dryer business, they also provide fabrication services for large equipment OEMs.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='uzelac-industries-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='VESCO-NM is based in Albuquerque, New Mexico. The company was founded in 2009 by Dr. Abdel-Rahman El-Emawy, who earned his Ph.D. from Colorado State University in 1996 with a dissertation on II/VI material growth by MBE. After joining the Center for High Technology Materials at the University of New Mexico as a research professor, he led MBE and MOCVD programs for quantum dots, dilute nitrides, and spintronic materials. His earlier career included work as an aircraft avionics engineer and development of GaAs-based BiFETs for telecommunications. Dr. El-Emawy founded VESCO-NM to commercialize his expertise in epitaxial growth equipment.

The company designs and manufactures proprietary molecular beam epitaxy (MBE) systems—such as the Ultima 310—and a range of MBE components including valved crackers, effusion cells, RF plasma sources, and tantalum-wire heaters. It also produces components for metal organic chemical vapor deposition (MOCVD) systems. In addition to new equipment, VESCO-NM provides decommissioning, decontamination, refurbishment, and installation services for semiconductor cleanroom tools worldwide. Its Albuquerque facility houses a machine shop with CNC milling, CNC turning, wire EDM, water jet cutting, and welding stations, plus a cleanroom for assembly and testing and CAD workstations for design and simulation.

VESCO-NM serves research institutions, universities, private industry, and government agencies across the globe. Its equipment supports applications in crystal growth, material deposition, LED manufacturing, renewable energy, thin-film technologies, and consumer electronics. The company reports more than 300 customers served worldwide.

The firm emphasizes four core values: quality in design and fabrication, value through reasonable pricing, customer service, and on-time delivery. It differentiates itself with proprietary source designs that achieve high flux uniformity, stability, and dissociation efficiency, all manufactured in-house under controlled conditions.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["MBE system manufacturing", "MBE component manufacturing", "MOCVD component manufacturing", "Semiconductor tool decommissioning", "Decontamination and cleaning services", "System installation", "System refurbishment", "CNC milling", "CNC turning", "Wire EDM", "Water jet cutting", "Welding", "Cleanroom assembly", "CAD design and simulation"], "industries": ["Research and development", "Higher education", "Private industry", "Government", "LED manufacturing", "Renewable energy", "Thin-film technology", "Consumer electronics"], "materials": ["III-V semiconductors", "II-VI semiconductors", "Antimony (Sb)", "Zinc (Zn)", "Selenium (Se)", "Cadmium (Cd)", "Cadmium telluride (CdTe)", "Tellurium (Te)", "Magnesium (Mg)", "Nitrides", "Oxides"], "equipment": ["CNC milling machines", "CNC lathes", "Wire EDM", "Water jet cutter", "Welding stations", "Cleanroom assembly area", "CAD design workstations", "VESCO Ultima 310 MBE system", "Valved crackers", "High-temperature effusion cells", "RF plasma sources", "MBE heaters"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary MBE system designs (e.g., Ultima 310)", "Valved crackers with high flux uniformity and stability", "Effusion cells engineered for reliability and longevity", "RF plasma sources with high dissociation efficiency for nitrides and oxides", "In-house machine shop and cleanroom for fabrication and assembly"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2009 by Dr. Abdel-Rahman El-Emawy -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Albuquerque, New Mexico -> /about-us, db", "Manufactures proprietary MBE systems and components -> /, /about-us", "Produces MOCVD components -> /, /about-us", "Provides decommissioning, decontamination, refurbishment, installation services -> /, /about-us", "Facility includes CNC milling, CNC lathe, wire EDM, water jet, welding, cleanroom, CAD workstations -> /about-us", "Serves research institutions, universities, private industry, government -> /about-us", "Applications: crystal growth, material deposition, LED manufacturing, renewable energy, thin-film technologies, consumer electronics -> /about-us", "300+ customers worldwide -> /", "40+ years of experience (collective) -> /", "Core values: Quality, Value, Service, Delivery -> /about-us", "Products: Ultima 310 MBE system, valved crackers, effusion cells, RF plasma sources, MBE heaters -> /", "Valved crackers used for Sb, Zn, Se, Cd, CdTe, Te, Mg -> /", "High-temperature effusion cells for low vapor pressure materials 1500-2000\u00b0C -> /", "RF plasma sources for nitrides and oxides -> /", "MBE heaters from 0.040\" OD tantalum wire -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "VESCO-NM manufactures state of the art proprietary Molecular Beam Epitaxy (MBE) systems and components as well as components for Metal Organic Chemical Vapor Deposition (MOCVD) systems.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vesco-nm' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company traces its roots to a Los Angeles landmark location and moved to a new facility in 2017.

The company designs and manufactures custom wire and cable, specializing in multi-conductor, composite, and coaxial constructions. Its product range includes custom sensor cables, outdoor data cables, harsh-environment cables, Mil-Spec cables, low-noise cables, UL-listed cables, RG174 coaxial cables, and application-specific cables for oil and gas, nuclear, robotics, travel, heater, and battery applications. Victor Wire & Cable operates a full range of wire and cable manufacturing equipment and is UL-certified.

Victor Wire & Cable serves industries including oil and gas, nuclear, robotics, travel, heating, and battery applications, providing custom cable solutions for demanding environments. The company also supports broader industrial applications with custom cable designs.

The company emphasizes its engineering assistance, adherence to high quality standards, and UL certification as key differentiators, with over 50 years of experience in custom cable design and manufacturing.', certifications=ARRAY['MIL SPEC','UL']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable design", "Custom cable manufacturing", "Mil-Spec cable production", "Low-noise cable production", "UL-listed cable production", "Coaxial cable manufacturing (RG174)", "Multi-conductor composite cable manufacturing", "Harsh-environment cable manufacturing", "Engineering assistance for cable solutions", "Oil & gas cable manufacturing", "Nuclear cable manufacturing", "Robotics cable manufacturing", "Travel cable manufacturing", "Heater cable manufacturing", "Battery cable manufacturing"], "industries": ["Oil & Gas", "Nuclear", "Robotics", "Travel", "Heating", "Battery", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 50 years of custom cable design and manufacturing experience", "UL-certified custom wire and cable manufacturer", "Specializes in multi-conductor, composite, and coaxial cables", "Offers engineering assistance for custom cable solutions", "MIL SPEC qualified"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1954 -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Los Angeles, California -> db", "UL-certified custom wire and cable manufacturer -> /", "Specializes in multi-conductor, composite, and coaxial cables -> /about-us", "Over 50 years of experience -> /about-us, /", "MIL SPEC capability -> db, /", "Offers engineering assistance -> /about-us", "Moved to new location in 2017 -> /about-us", "Products include custom sensor cables, outdoor data cables, harsh environment cables -> /", "Industries served: oil & gas, nuclear, robotics, travel, heating, battery -> /", "Full range of wire and cable manufacturing equipment -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Victor Wire & Cable is a Custom Wire & Cable manufacturer specializing in unique Multi-Conductor, Composite and Coaxial Cables.", "founded_year": "1954", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='victor-wire-cable' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='VRG Components, Inc. was founded in 2014 in Matthews, North Carolina, with the mission of supplying electronics manufacturers with high-quality components to maximize their production processes. The company operates as an independent worldwide distributor of electronic components, semiconductors, and network components.

The distributor specializes in global sourcing services for new, allocated, end-of-life, last-time-buy, and long-lead-time electronic components from over 500 manufacturers across more than 50 product lines, with over 50,000 parts available. Its multi-lingual sourcing team leverages over 50 years of combined industry expertise to fill supply gaps for customers worldwide.

VRG serves automotive tier suppliers, electronic manufacturing services providers, and contract manufacturers, as well as medical device manufacturers, transportation systems builders, machinery manufacturers, and telecommunications and consumer electronics companies. Customers turn to the company when primary suppliers cannot deliver crucial components.

The company distinguishes itself through its AS9120-certified quality management system, a commitment to quote turnaround within 30 minutes, and a global inventory network that provides access to hard-to-find parts. It also holds authorized distributor status for brands such as wenglor sensoric, Lutronic, and Lumberg.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9120']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Global sourcing of electronic components", "Authorized distribution", "Obsolete and end-of-life component sourcing", "Long lead time component sourcing", "Supply chain gap fulfillment", "Fast quote turnaround (30 minutes)"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Medical Electronics", "Transportation", "Machinery", "Telecommunications", "Consumer Electronics"], "materials": ["Electronic components", "Semiconductors", "Network components", "Electrical components and spare parts"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Quote turnaround within 30 minutes", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["AS9120-certified quality management system", "Multi-lingual sourcing team (German, Spanish)", "Global sourcing network with 500+ manufacturers", "Quote turnaround within 30 minutes", "50+ years combined industry expertise"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2014 -> db", "Headquarters in Matthews, North Carolina -> db", "Independent worldwide distributor of electronic components, semiconductors, and network components -> /", "Specializes in global sourcing for new, allocated, end-of-life, last-time-buy, and long-lead-time components -> /", "Over 500 manufacturers, 50+ product lines, 50,000+ parts available -> /", "50+ years of combined industry expertise -> /", "Multi-lingual team speaking German and Spanish -> /", "AS9120 certified -> /", "Serves automotive, medical electronics, transportation, machinery, telecommunications, consumer electronics -> /", "Authorized distributor for wenglor sensoric, Lutronic, Lumberg -> /", "Quote turnaround within 30 minutes -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "VRG Components\u00ae is an industry-leading, AS9120 certified, independent worldwide distributor of electronic components, semiconductors, and network components from hundreds of product manufacturers.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["German", "Spanish"], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='vrg-components-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Valley Services Electronics (VSE) operates from San Jose, California, with a second facility in Reno, Nevada. The company has been providing printed circuit board assembly and electronics manufacturing services for over forty years, though a specific founding year is not disclosed. Ownership details and founder names are not publicly stated; the business presents itself as a U.S.-based contract manufacturer serving the Silicon Valley ecosystem.

VSE delivers end-to-end electronics manufacturing, spanning PCBA design and engineering (including DFM/DFT support), prototype and low-volume assembly, high-mix mid-volume production, and full turnkey box-build and cable-harness integration. Its San Jose site focuses on new product introduction (NPI) and quick-turn prototypes, while the Reno facility handles higher-volume runs.

The customer base spans aerospace, biotechnology, telecommunications, semiconductor, medical devices, clean technology, automotive, renewable energy, and industrial equipment sectors. VSE works directly with design teams, supply-chain departments, and original equipment manufacturers that require regulatory compliance (ITAR, ISO 13485) and domestic manufacturing for mission-critical applications.

The company emphasizes five operational pillars: scalable production with a boutique approach, supply-chain resilience through vertical integration and domestic assembly, speed to market via streamlined handoffs and direct communication, secure transparent partnerships protecting intellectual property, and total quality built around IPC and ISO standards. Its stated mission is to empower life-changing technologies worldwide by unifying engineering, assembly, and testing in a single streamlined process.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','ITAR','RoHS','IPC 610']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCBA Design Services", "PCBA Engineering Services (DFM/DFT)", "PCB Assembly (PCBA)", "Low-Volume PCB Assembly", "NPI (New Product Introduction) PCB Assembly", "High-Volume PCB Assembly", "Turnkey PCB Assembly", "Box Build Assembly", "Wire Harness & Cable Assembly", "Custom Electronic Enclosures", "In-Circuit Testing", "Functional Testing", "Environmental Testing", "HIPOT Testing", "X-Ray Inspection", "PCB Prototyping", "Supply Chain Management / Strategic Sourcing", "Component Procurement", "Obsolescence Management (Form Fit Function)", "Multilayer PCBA", "Rigid-Flex PCBA", "HDI PCBA", "High-Speed PCBA", "RoHS Compliant Assembly", "PCBA Service Bureau (schematic to board file)"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Biotechnology", "Telecommunications", "Semiconductor", "Medical Devices", "Clean Technology", "Automotive", "Renewable Energy", "Industrial Equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Facilities in San Jose (NPI) and Reno (high-volume production)", "Over 40 years of PCBA manufacturing experience", "ISO 9001, ISO 13485, ITAR, and IPC 610 compliance", "Vertically integrated supply chain with domestic assembly", "Quick-turn prototyping and scalable low- to high-volume production"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in San Jose, CA and Reno, NV -> /about, /services", 