UPDATE companies SET description='Vital Farms’ Egg Central Station operates in Springfield, Missouri. The facility was established in 2015 as part of Vital Farms, a company that traces its roots to 2007 when its founders set out to prove that animal welfare, family farms, and food quality could scale together. The business is structured as a certified B Corporation and operates under a stakeholder model that considers farmers, animals, crew members, stockholders, the environment, community, vendors, and consumers.

The plant handles multiple product lines including pasture-raised, organic, restorative, and True Blues eggs, as well as hard-boiled and liquid whole eggs. The company reports 39,000-plus acres of pasture rotated annually and distribution to roughly 24,000 retailers nationwide.

