UPDATE companies SET description='Vital Plastics, LLC was founded in 1994 in Baldwin, Wisconsin, located east of the Twin Cities metro area along Interstate 94. The company operates two manufacturing facilities in Baldwin and has grown to become a custom plastic injection molding and assembly solutions provider.

Its 70,000 square feet of climate-controlled manufacturing space houses a cellular manufacturing model and leverages RJG scientific molding practices alongside IQMS integration for real-time production monitoring. Beyond molding, Vital Plastics offers comprehensive assembly services including automated, semi-automated, and hand-set assembly, heat staking, hot stamping, ultrasonic welding, pad printing, and kitting. Tooling solutions cover maintenance, design, modifications, and warehousing, while the quality lab provides CMM inspection, optical comparators, and PPAP documentation up to Level 5.

Vital Plastics serves multiple industries and has supplied Fortune 1000 companies since 2009. Its engineering expertise spans prototype through production runs, with materials ranging from commodity and engineered grades to filled, unfilled, and high-temperature exotic resins. The company also supports metal-to-plastic conversion projects.

