UPDATE companies SET description='Ward''s Manufacturing operates from Warren, Rhode Island, where siblings Kiffin and Kelly Ward founded the company in 2022. The woman-owned, millennial-owned business began after the pair experienced firsthand the difficulties of sourcing reliable domestic metal fabrication and decided to fill that gap themselves, drawing on a family legacy of tradespeople and a commitment to U.S.-based production.

The shop provides custom metal fabrication including fiber laser cutting, CNC press brake bending, machining, finishing, and product design. Its equipment includes a 3 kW fiber optic laser with a 5-by-10-foot bed capable of cutting mild steel up to 3/4 inch, stainless up to 3/8 inch, and aluminum up to 5/16 inch, plus a 190-ton CNC press brake that bends parts up to 10 feet long. In-house finishing covers #4 brushed, vibratory tumbling, glass bead blasting, and orbital sanding, while value-added services range from powder coating and anodizing to welding, assembly, and heat treating. The company reports a 99% quality rate and handles orders from single prototypes to production runs of tens of thousands of units with no minimum order quantity.

Ward''s serves customers across aerospace and defense, marine, robotics and automation, renewable energy (solar frames, wind turbine components), medical devices, electronics enclosures, and industrial equipment. Concrete examples include aircraft components, marine-grade corrosion-resistant parts, robotic sensor components, solar panel frames, wind energy parts, medical-grade metal parts, and electronic enclosures and brackets. The company has shipped to 43 U.S. states and four Canadian provinces.

The founders started the business to address the lack of responsive, high-quality domestic fabrication options they encountered as buyers. They emphasize short lead times — including 24- to 48-hour expedited delivery — flexible scheduling, responsive communication, and the supply-chain security of all-U.S. production. Woman-owned (WBE-certified) and Green Manufacturer certifications help clients meet supplier diversity and sustainability goals.', certifications=ARRAY['WBE-certified','Green Manufacturer certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fiber laser cutting", "CNC press brake bending", "Machining (thread cutting, countersinking, counterboring, reaming, inserts, laser etching)", "Finishing (#4 brushed, vibratory tumbling, glass bead blasting, orbital sanding)", "Product design & engineering support (CAD file creation, design optimization, GD&T)", "Powder coating", "Wet painting", "Anodizing", "Assembly", "Welding", "Electropolishing", "Black oxidizing", "Hardcoating", "Heat treating", "Passivating", "Teflon impregnation and coating", "Chromating", "Chemical conversion coating", "Electroless plating", "Electroplating", "Hardening", "Metal carbonitriding", "Annealing", "Thur-Hardening tempering"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Defense", "Marine / Boat Building", "Robotics & Automation", "Renewable Energy (Solar, Wind)", "Medical Devices", "Electronics Enclosures", "Industrial Equipment", "Aviation", "Industrial Automation", "Autonomous Underwater Vehicles (AUVs)", "Unmanned Underwater Vehicles (UUVs)", "Unmanned Aircraft Systems (UAS)", "Composites", "Machinery", "Sports Equipment", "Furniture Making", "Art & Jewelry", "Industrial Design", "Custom Signage", "Shellfish Aquaculture", "Metal Forming", "Metrology", "Automotive"], "materials": ["Mild steel", "Stainless steel", "Aluminum", "Brass", "Copper", "Titanium", "Nickel"], "equipment": ["3 kW Fiber Optic Laser Cutter (5'' x 10'' bed)", "190-ton CNC Press Brake (10 ft capacity)"], "volume": "Prototype t