UPDATE companies SET description='Wayne Mills has operated in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania since 1910. The family-owned business, now in its fifth generation, began weaving twill tapes and light webbings when steam was coal-fired and yarn arrived by horse-drawn wagon.

Today the company runs a 150,000-square-foot complex of nine buildings on four acres in the city''s historic Germantown district. More than 60 employees—many with decades of tenure—operate warping and weaving machines, a high-speed bleaching range, a computer-controlled Mageba continuous dye line, and 16 skein dyeing machines. The facility also houses custom coating, reflective lamination, and cutting/packaging lines. Stock items such as cotton tapes (styles 6210, 5541, 5526, 4214, 5533) ship quickly, while custom orders are fulfilled with the same attention to detail.

The narrow fabrics serve apparel, bag and strap makers, military-specification programs, and safety applications requiring reflective lamination. Customers include Analog Watch Company and public-sector buyers such as the Philadelphia Commerce Department.

Wayne Mills differentiates itself with a 15-pound minimum for custom dye lots—far below the industry''s typical 500- to 1,000-pound threshold—and an in-house quality lab that tests break strength, elongation, wash fastness, and adhesive performance. Environmental awards recognize its wastewater treatment, and the firm emphasizes U.S. manufacturing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Textile design", "Narrow fabric bleaching", "Custom dyeing and lab dips", "Reflective lamination", "Custom coating (including pressure-sensitive adhesive)", "Custom cutting, put-ups, and packaging", "Warping", "Weaving", "Continuous bleaching", "Continuous dyeing (Mageba)", "Skein dyeing", "Quality control lab testing (break strength, elongation, wash fastness, thermoplastic adhesive performance)", "Wastewater treatment (environmental compliance)"], "industries": ["Apparel", "Bindings", "Military specification", "Bags and straps", "Safety/high-visibility", "Specialty trades"], "materials": ["Cotton", "Polyester", "Nylon"], "equipment": ["Warping machines", "Weaving machines", "High-speed bleaching range", "Computer-controlled Mageba continuous dye range", "16 skein dyeing machines", "Two natural gas-fired boilers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["15-pound minimum for custom dye lots", "Extensive stock inventory enabling fast turnaround", "In-house dyehouse with 16 skein machines and Mageba continuous range", "Over 60 long-tenured employees (many 25+ years)", "Family-owned fifth generation with deep process knowledge"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1910, family-owned fifth generation -> /about", "Philadelphia, Pennsylvania location -> /about", "150,000 sq ft facility, 9 buildings, 4 acres -> /about", "60+ employees, many 25+ years tenure -> /about", "Warping, weaving, continuous bleaching, continuous dyeing (Mageba), 16 skein dyeing machines -> /about, /services", "Two natural gas-fired boilers -> /about", "Stock cotton tape styles 621