UPDATE companies SET description='Established in 2008, the Western Washington Sheet Metal Joint Apprenticeship Training Committee (JATC) operates as a non-profit labor-management partnership headquartered in Everett, Washington, with a second campus in DuPont. The committee was formed by the Sheet Metal Air, Rail and Transportation Workers (SMART) Local 66 and the Sheet Metal and Air Conditioning Contractors'' Association (SMACNA) Western Washington to provide standardized apprenticeship training for the region''s sheet metal industry. While union apprenticeship in the trade dates back over a century, the modern JATC structure has been in place since 1973.

The JATC delivers tuition-free apprenticeship programs in four core disciplines: sheet metal fabrication and installation, testing adjusting and balancing (TAB), HVAC service, and residential sheet metal. Training combines on-the-job placement with one of 72 signatory contractors—ranging from small shops to large mechanical firms such as MacDonald-Miller, Hermanson Company, and McKinstry—with classroom and lab instruction at the two campuses. The center employs 12 full-time staff, including seven instructors with a combined 210 years of industry experience, and typically enrolls roughly 500 apprentices, graduating about 98 journey-level workers annually.

Graduates enter the commercial construction, HVAC, and building trades sectors, with notable project experience in healthcare facilities, smoke control systems, and energy-efficient heat pump installations recognized by the U.S. Department of Energy. The DuPont campus hosts the SMART Heroes program, which provides a direct entry pathway for active-duty military personnel and veterans. Apprentices earn competitive wages—starting at $70,520 annually with full benefits including retirement, medical, dental, and vision—while incurring zero student debt and receiving credit toward an associate degree.

The JATC''s governing board comprises six labor trustees and six management trustees, ensuring curriculum aligns with contractor needs. Instructors bring field expertise from major projects for clients such as Microsoft, SpaceX, Costco, and regional healthcare systems, and hold certifications including WABO welding, TABB, and NEMI/ICB credentials. The program''s mission centers on producing a highly skilled, competitive workforce through joint labor-management collaboration.', certifications=ARRAY['WABO welding certification','TABB certification','NEMI/ICB certification','U.S. Department of Energy Energy Skilled recognition (Heat Pump Installation)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sheet metal apprenticeship training", "Testing, adjusting, and balancing (TAB) training", "HVAC service apprenticeship training", "Residential sheet metal training", "Welding certification (WABO)", "SMART Heroes veteran apprenticeship pathway", "On-the-job training placement", "Classroom and lab instruction", "Blueprint reading and layout training", "Commissioning and controls training", "Energy auditing training", "Bluebeam software training", "Mechanical systems troubleshooting training"], "industries": ["Sheet metal fabrication", "HVAC", "Commercial construction", "Testing, adjusting, and balancing (TAB)", "Healthcare facilities", "Smoke control systems", "Energy efficiency / heat pump installation", "Veteran workforce development", "Building trades"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Free apprenticeship training with zero student debt", "Competitive apprentice wages and benefits from day one", "SMART Heroes veteran transition program at DuPont campus", "Joint labor-management governance with 72 contractor training agents", "DOE Energy Skilled recognition for heat pump installation training"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2008 -> db", "Headquarters Everett, WA -> db, /about", "Second campus DuPont, WA -> /about", "Non-profit union training center -> /about", "Formed by SMART Local 66 and SMACNA Western Washington -> /about", "Modern apprenticeship since 1973 -> /about", "Four core training disciplines: sheet metal, TAB, HVAC service, residential sheet metal -> /about", "72 signatory contractors (training agents) -> /about", "Contractor examples: MacDonald-Miller, Hermanson Company, McKinstry -> /about, /", "12 full-time staff (3 admin, 2 support, 7 instructors) -> /about", "Combined 210 years instructor experience -> /about", "~500 apprentices enrolled, ~98 graduates annually -> /about", "SMART Heroes program for veterans at DuPont campus -> /about", "Apprentice wages: Year 1 $70,520, Year 3 $86,840, Year 5 $115,780 -> /", "Benefits: Retirement, Family Medical, Dental, & Vision -> /, /about", "Zero student debt, credit toward AAS degree -> /", "DOE Energy Skilled recognition for heat pump installation -> /, /about", "Governing board: 6 labor trustees, 6 management trustees -> /about", "Instructor certifications: WABO, TABB, NEMI/ICB -> /about", "Instructor project experience: Microsoft, SpaceX, Costco, healthcare -> /about", "Mission: bring Labor and Management together for skilled workforce -> /about"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "The Western Washington Sheet Metal Joint Apprenticeship Training Committee (JATC) is a top-notch non-profit union training center serving all Western Washington.", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "12", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='western-washington-sheet-metal' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Westfield Sheet Metal Works, Inc. has operated in Kenilworth, New Jersey since 1928 as a union shop affiliated with Sheet Metal Workers Union Local 22. The company occupies a 50,000-square-foot manufacturing and office facility on a 100,000-square-foot lot at North 8th Street and Monroe Avenue.

The shop provides custom metal fabrication from design through installation, handling projects that range from small machine guards to 10-by-10-foot plenums requiring crane lifts. In-house capabilities include engineering and project management, shearing, bending, welding, polishing, painting, quality control, and delivery, all coordinated from CAD drawings or sketches.

The firm serves architectural, commercial, construction, and manufacturing clients. Completed projects include the Streicker Bridge, light pylons for Gantry Plaza, structural elements for Hunters Point South Park, Madison Square Garden, and Hunts Point Landing.

