UPDATE companies SET description='Westshore Electronics was founded in 2003 in Holland, Michigan. The company began as an engineering-focused firm providing electronic and mechanical design alongside software development.

The company operates as a contract electronics manufacturer offering a full range of services from concept through production. Its capabilities include double-sided surface-mount assembly, flexible and metal-core PCB assembly, through-hole and mixed-technology assembly, automated selective wave soldering, fine-pitch component placement down to 01005 packages, BGA placement, conformal coating, microcontroller programming, and 100% functional testing.

Westshore serves small and mid-tier manufacturers in the medical, industrial controls, durable goods, and inspection lighting sectors. Customers typically require embedded control systems, high-density circuit boards, LED PCBAs, instrument lighting, and electromechanical controls.

